= The Militia Threat

Armed militias, sometimes in uniform, show up at protests, state capitols, and polling places. Their numbers are small but growing, and some officials are tolerating them.

- @militia_ban: Demand the law be enforced
- @militia_civic: Build a civic counterweight
- @militia_shrug: Downplay it

@militia_ban
on-arrival: militia_done = 1; farright_strength -= 4; militia_strength -= 100; federal_law_loyalty += 0.02; polarization += 1; maga_strength -= 1

Prosecutors move; militia numbers fall.

@militia_civic
on-arrival: militia_done = 1; civic_strength += 600; election_admin += 3; dem_enthusiasm += 0.3; radicalization += 1

Volunteers organize to protect polling places and officials.

@militia_shrug
on-arrival: militia_done = 1; farright_strength += 2; militia_strength += 60; pro_democracy -= 2

Downplaying the threat does nothing to reduce it.
